/**
 * @mainpage MiniDevil documentation
 * 
 * @section intro What is MiniDevil?
 * 
 * MiniDevil is a POSIX inspired shell written in C as a 42 school project.\n
 * It reads a line from terminal then breaks it into tokens and parses them
 * into an AST (Abstract Syntax Tree) & executes the tree.\n 
 * 
 * @section diagram How does it work?
 * 
 * \image html pipeline.svg
 * 
 * @section entry Entry point
 * 
 * main() in src/main.c initialises t_shell, calls main_loop().\n
 * main_loop() is a REPL that sets up signals, reads one line of input,
 * passes it to handle_input(), frees it, and repeats until the shell exits.
 * 
 * @section nav Where to start
 * 
 * - [**File list**](files.html)
 * - @ref signals "Signal handling strategy"
 * - @ref execution_model "Execution model" 
 * - @ref memory_ownership "Memory ownership rules"
 * - @ref fd_lifecycle "File descriptors lifecycle"
 * - @ref exit_statuses "Exit status rules"
 * 
 * @section modules Module index
 * 
 * - @ref grp_lexer "Lexer (Tokenizer + expander)"
 * - @ref grp_parser "Parser (AST construction)"
 * - @ref grp_executor "Executor (commands, pipes & redirections)"
 * - @ref grp_builtins "Builtin commands"
 * - @ref grp_env "Environment management"
 * - @ref grp_signals "Signal handling"
 * - @ref grp_ui "UI Mode (optional)"
 * 
